                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "this game was my GF's favorite game to play and wanted to play it with me so i boot it up and the game started out fun all things considered but after like 20 hours the game got incredibly repetitive and clunkier as time went on like the devs stop the QA checks after a while. lemme do a list of the good and the bad\n\nThe GOOD:\nInteresting combat system where prioritizing the weak points is fun because i get to practice my aim.\n\nThe crafting and survival elements are pretty cool and do their job well to immerse you in the world's atmosphere.\n\nEach weapons use case feels unique enough to warrant choosing which weapons you want to take with you.\n\nRewards for beating up bases and elites are well worth the investment in time and effort.\n\nThe Pet you can obtain later in the game is a hoot and a holler to use. No notes.\n\nThe Physics engine is really fun to goof off in if you find yourself in possession of like 20 propane tanks\n\nThe special optic sight modifiers (Night vision, Therma, Object Penetration) are all rally cool (Object Penetration is the best of the 3 IMO)\n\n\n\n\nThe BAD:\nThe gameplay loop stagnates HARD after like 4 hours and it boils down to this(Go to place, loot, fight bots nearby, leave to got to new place or complete mission. REPEAT)\nThe gunplay is clunky and doesn't feel good to use in longer engagements (which is most of them in the late game)\n \nThe Protype Tier 6 guns are a grab bag of useful or lame and have wild ranges of actual viability. Examples include the pump shotgun T6 which is dependent in the ammo used in it to get the most out of it (which isn't much), an LMG with an overheat mechanic which is cool but means it has the same uptime of a normal LMG if you don't manage the heat masterfully which isn't ideal and the SMG which is a smart weapon that cannot miss and aims where you first ADS the robot at which makes it superb for shredding weak points and is easily among the best weapons I've used from this Tier\n\nThe DLCs Feel lackluster and don't do much for the grand story at large and the weapon DLC feel like just a way to make money off the people who wouldn't buy the Story DLC and as a result feel cheap.\n\nThe story is kinda whatever. its not bad or good but its fumbling beats left and right and delivers a good-ish story poorly. If anything, the story barely keeps people playing the first time through and when you get to the end its sort of a nothing burger that only serves to let you continue playing the game\n\nThe vehicles in this game are useless minus the bicycle because it doesn't require gas to function.\n\nThe same Pet you can obtain that i glazed is also a serial armor waster and will actively run in, stand still, take 99% of its armor in damage and then fire off ONE shot that does some amount of damage you don't get to know about because....\n\nThe game has a minimalist HUD which in most games i can appreciate but it feels like ,in some cases at least, a little more info is needed. For example, when fighting bigger robots you will see them break down over the course of the fight but when it looks like its about to go down, it just...keeps living. this is most apparent on the apocalypse class of enemies where they feel like they just wont die and your fighting them for like 3 minutes longer than you have to.\n\nThis is kind of a nitpick but the Dot reticles in this game are really lazy. they are a opaque red dot on the front glass and that bothers me a lot. on top of that, the quality system in this game make all but the last two rarity of dot sight even usable with how dirty and cracked the other ones are.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTL;DR Its fun if you have someone to play with but it has too many glaring issues for someone like me to recommend anyone get this game unless it was like 80% off and then you can just goof off in a robo apocalypse landscape and have fun for a good few hours with a buddy or two and now you have some fun memories for real cheap",
